# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Utilities map (reuse before you write)

**Read this file BEFORE writing new code.** Each row is a helper, base class, hook, composable or
generic function that already exists: consume it, never write a variant of it. Before changing one,
check who consumes it in the census of the project's `usage-map.md`.

How the file is kept: each project block opens with a `map-refresh: scan` marker comment that names
the scan date and the project. Its rows regenerate on every refresh; the ✍ columns are human text
and the refresh preserves them. Edit only the ✍ cells, the Curated table and the Retired table.
Consumers is the number of files that use the symbol, shown as a bucket: `0 · 1 · 2–5 · 6–20 · 20+`.

